    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sedalia opened its first post office on March 5, 1879, with John Morris as the inaugural postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sedalia_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1880, Sedalia boasted general stores, a blacksmith shop, a mill, and a part‑time barbershop and dentist’s office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sedalia_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Great Flood of 1937 and a 2023 flash flood highlighted Sedalia’s vulnerability to Ohio River basin flooding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        3,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sedalia_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sedalia enjoys a humid subtropical climate, with summer highs near 90°F, winter lows around 26°F, and about 53 inches of yearly rain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
